    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0621" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg526"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13775: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-16T17:00:00+08:00">December 16, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 16—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>618. Hankow’s December 15, 5 p.m.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d556-f1"/> Embassy here
                    telegraphed this morning to an American missionary in Sian, requesting him to
                    report by telegraph concerning safety and welfare of American citizens in Sian
                    and vicinity.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d556-f2"/> Telegraph office here accepted
                    message and will endeavor to ascertain whether it is delivered. Telegraph line
                    is reported open to Sian but messages are subject to delay in delivery and
                    censorship.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department, Nanking, Shanghai and Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d556-f1" n="90" xml:id="d556-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d556-f2" n="91" xml:id="d556-f2-content">
                <p>This request followed the seizure of Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek by mutinous
                    military leaders at Sian.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
